OrionLayer open fix 82 — a beam's aim as a battle event
=======================================================

Work order 213 (point D, Data's decision of 4 October 2026: an engine change a
point needs is made and applied in the same run). orion2re on
`orionlayer-local`, on top of open fix 71, amended. Every line under
ORION2RE_EXT.

`Beam_SFX_` (beams.cpp:1294-1712) draws each entry of a FIRE from a fire point
of the shooter's picture (FIREPTS) to the target's centre plus, for a miss, two
`Random_` offsets (:1381-1443); its frame count halves its step past six frames
(:2287-2301), so a few pixels decide the beat. Neither point was on the wire
(work order 212: an Ion Pulse Cannon miss ran 4 passes in the original and 7 in
HD). Where the loop starts an entry (its frame 0, the last fire point drawn)
CEV_BEAM_AIM is recorded: the shooter, the target, the weapon, the fire points,
the start and the end point in world px. Not for a reflected beam (its own
loop, reflection state 2). `Combat_Note` records it without restarting open fix
79's tick count, so the sounds after it keep counting from the event they belong
to.

